## Trade-off Summary

| Solution | Pros | Cons | Best For |
|----------|------|------|----------|
| **U8g2_for_Adafruit_GFX** | Drop-in, no font work needed | Bitmap only, limited styles | Quick integration with existing Adafruit_GFX code |
| **TFT_eSPI + .vlw fonts** | Smooth anti-aliased, fast, native UTF-8 | Requires flash storage, setup overhead | Production UI needing polished rendering |
| **ASCII conversion** | Zero overhead, simple | Loses all diacritics/meaning | Debug displays, non-critical info |
| **Custom GFXfont** | Full control over styling | Manual UTF-8 decoder, large files | When locked into Adafruit_GFX ecosystem |

**Recommendation**: Use **TFT_eSPI with .vlw smooth fonts** for the GC9A01 round display. It provides native Vietnamese UTF-8 support with beautiful anti-aliased rendering and is the fastest path to production-quality results.
